  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "The records repeatedly establish high-energy mechanical alloying of elemental HEA powders under argon followed by vacuum SPS as a route to dense, fine- or nanocrystalline bulk alloys. Several use short SPS holds, and R9 is especially close to the later paper's 1 h milling and 1000 °C processing window. R1 and R4 further show that milling plus SPS can generate mixed FCC/BCC structures, while R1, R4, R5, and related records connect fine grains, solid solutions, and milling-generated defects or precipitates to high hardness and compressive strength through grain-boundary and solid-solution strengthening. Although the exact CoCrFeNiTi composition, FCC/BCC ratio, and Ti-specific thermodynamic explanation are not disclosed, an expert could plausibly combine these teachings to propose the later intervention and its principal strengthening mechanism."
